WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.476 --> 00:00:03.733
- Life's so short and such
glorious images in the world

00:00:03.733 --> 00:00:05.612
and such horror as well

00:00:05.612 --> 00:00:06.833
that I want to see it all.

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:08.433
I know people who live in the past,

00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:10.767
they just live back there all the time,

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.937
talk about something that
happens to them 30 years ago,

00:00:12.937 --> 00:00:14.571
they're like zombies.

00:00:14.571 --> 00:00:16.949
Be bold and mighty forces
will come to your aid

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:18.424
and I believe that about everything.

00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:20.643
We have to make our lives
because life is tough,

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:23.750
we have to believe in the power of life.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.339
- He's a Welsh actor on
film, stage and television.

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:29.101
He's considered to be one of the world's

00:00:29.101 --> 00:00:30.943
greatest living actors

00:00:30.943 --> 00:00:33.498
and is most well known for
his role as Hannibal Lecter

00:00:33.498 --> 00:00:35.881
in the Silence of the Lambs.

00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:37.400
- Every thing you need to find him

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.882
is right there in those pages.

00:00:38.882 --> 00:00:41.500
- Since 2016 he's starred
in the critically acclaimed

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.556
HBO series, Westworld.

00:00:43.556 --> 00:00:45.483
He's Anthony Hopkins and here's my take

00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.621
on his top 10 rules to success.

00:00:47.621 --> 00:00:49.351
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:49.351 --> 00:00:51.436
and I'm super curious
to figure out which one

00:00:51.436 --> 00:00:52.701
you guys like the best.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.099
Also as you're watching the clips

00:00:54.099 --> 00:00:55.779
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:55.779 --> 00:00:57.442
please it down in the comments below

00:00:57.442 --> 00:00:59.894
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired

00:00:59.894 --> 00:01:01.859
as well when you write something down

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:05.492
it's much more likely
to stick with you too.

00:01:05.492 --> 00:01:06.325
Enjoy.

00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:13.112
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:19.132 --> 00:01:20.650
- Do something new,

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.407
you know you've got to, you
can't stay in your comfort zone,

00:01:23.407 --> 00:01:24.240
that's what we all do.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.588
We get to a certain age and we
all stay in our comfort zone

00:01:26.588 --> 00:01:29.124
in our recliners watching
television, day in and day out,

00:01:29.124 --> 00:01:30.851
and when you get to a certain age,

00:01:30.851 --> 00:01:32.246
I'm going to be 70 at the end of the year,

00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:34.157
why sit around watching
television for the rest of my life

00:01:34.157 --> 00:01:36.731
cause I've done it all,
sitting on my laurel wreaths.

00:01:36.731 --> 00:01:39.191
It's not worth it, I mean life's so short

00:01:39.191 --> 00:01:42.078
and such glorious images in the world,

00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:43.924
and such horror as well,

00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:45.699
that I want to see it all,

00:01:45.699 --> 00:01:47.274
so I've moved out of my comfort zone.

00:01:47.274 --> 00:01:51.413
It's essential for me,
otherwise I may as well die.

00:01:51.413 --> 00:01:55.011
So I've done it, I've broken
every rule in the book,

00:01:55.011 --> 00:01:58.387
and not out of malice
or any telling anyone

00:01:58.387 --> 00:02:01.669
that I'll show you, I
did it to show myself.

00:02:01.669 --> 00:02:03.512
I've shown myself, I looked in the mirror

00:02:03.512 --> 00:02:04.908
and thought, I'll show you one day

00:02:04.908 --> 00:02:06.144
and I've done something completely new,

00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:09.297
I wrote the music and feel limitless.

00:02:09.297 --> 00:02:12.629
Once I got started with two magicians

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:15.296
and one ventriloquist helped me,

00:02:16.286 --> 00:02:18.655
once I got the knack of it,

00:02:18.655 --> 00:02:20.374
it became easier and then I enjoyed it.

00:02:20.374 --> 00:02:22.345
There were moments when
I was learning the script

00:02:22.345 --> 00:02:23.782
and I thought well this
isn't going to work,

00:02:23.782 --> 00:02:25.626
I mean, how can I do it?

00:02:25.626 --> 00:02:27.545
I used to write notes to myself,

00:02:27.545 --> 00:02:29.712
little letters to myself
and put them on the desk

00:02:29.712 --> 00:02:31.759
saying, you know, "You can do anything,

00:02:31.759 --> 00:02:34.680
"with faith you can move mountains.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.935
"Trust and let go."

00:02:36.935 --> 00:02:38.615
and all that sort of thing, you know

00:02:38.615 --> 00:02:40.138
and I just threw myself into it

00:02:40.138 --> 00:02:42.400
and when the negatives came to my mind

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.485
I would, I would make
positive sounds in my head,

00:02:46.485 --> 00:02:49.107
I'd say I can do it, you know.

00:02:49.107 --> 00:02:53.099
I used to meditate and
visualize myself doing it.

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:56.502
I still visualize myself
on like a kind of,

00:02:56.502 --> 00:02:59.453
trying to visual myself doing
those sort of fanning cards

00:02:59.453 --> 00:03:02.089
and spinning them and gradually,

00:03:02.089 --> 00:03:03.521
it's surprising the power of mind,

00:03:03.521 --> 00:03:05.897
what happens you know, your
muscles begin to respond.

00:03:05.897 --> 00:03:07.984
It's like anything really,
if you're playing the piano

00:03:07.984 --> 00:03:10.776
or driving the car, it
comes through relaxation.

00:03:10.776 --> 00:03:12.384
- [Audience Member] Your approach to life,

00:03:12.384 --> 00:03:14.929
has it changed through
your acting experience?

00:03:14.929 --> 00:03:17.305
- Yes, whether you just get older

00:03:17.305 --> 00:03:19.961
and you live long enough you change,

00:03:19.961 --> 00:03:21.476
(audience laughing)

00:03:21.476 --> 00:03:22.457
if you don't you may as well die.

00:03:22.457 --> 00:03:24.257
(audience laughing)

00:03:24.257 --> 00:03:26.346
You know, go or grow,

00:03:26.346 --> 00:03:27.846
you have to change

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:30.627
and I've realized over the years

00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:34.544
that I've gone through
many changes in my life.

00:03:35.451 --> 00:03:38.641
Many changes, because
that's the nature of life

00:03:38.641 --> 00:03:40.947
and if you don't go with it

00:03:40.947 --> 00:03:43.890
you may as well die, really,
you may as well be dead.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.321
I know people who live in the past,

00:03:45.321 --> 00:03:47.571
they just live there all the time,

00:03:47.571 --> 00:03:49.995
talk about something that
happens to them 30 years ago.

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:51.590
They're like zombies

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.268
and I can't hang out with those people,

00:03:53.268 --> 00:03:54.127
I know them

00:03:54.127 --> 00:03:55.840
but I can't spend more
than five minutes with them

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.651
because I feel like
suicide at the end of it

00:03:57.651 --> 00:03:59.704
because I feel so guilty about being happy

00:03:59.704 --> 00:04:01.019
when they're so miserable.

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:02.985
(audience laughing)

00:04:02.985 --> 00:04:05.030
Because life is in session,

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.900
for many years I thought
life was a big rehearsal

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.944
for the big event and
somebody in Los Angeles said,

00:04:10.944 --> 00:04:14.857
"Tony, this is the big
event, life is in session."

00:04:14.857 --> 00:04:17.434
You know we spend so much
time thinking into rehearsal

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:21.994
for the big event, the
big, red carpet in the sky

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.757
and there's not.

00:04:23.757 --> 00:04:27.077
All life is magical, it is magic you see

00:04:27.077 --> 00:04:29.451
because we're the instruments

00:04:29.451 --> 00:04:31.543
and all the problems are technical,

00:04:31.543 --> 00:04:33.912
once you can go through those problems

00:04:33.912 --> 00:04:36.087
without avoiding them or
backing off from them,

00:04:36.087 --> 00:04:40.107
because you know it's like
fear, you go through it,

00:04:40.107 --> 00:04:42.239
you go through the problem,
confront it and go through it,

00:04:42.239 --> 00:04:43.597
then you have release.

00:04:43.597 --> 00:04:45.075
Stanislavsky called it
the plane of inspiration

00:04:45.075 --> 00:04:46.763
that takes off the runway,
the runway is the technique,

00:04:46.763 --> 00:04:48.321
the runway is the getting on with it

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.628
and the plane will take off.

00:04:49.628 --> 00:04:51.711
If on Tuesday night however
it doesn't quite take off,

00:04:51.711 --> 00:04:53.353
it doesn't matter, you can't
stop the plane and say,

00:04:53.353 --> 00:04:55.154
"Well I'll go back cause
I don't feel it tonight."

00:04:55.154 --> 00:04:56.586
You get on with it technically

00:04:56.586 --> 00:04:57.815
and then on Wednesday night,

00:04:57.815 --> 00:04:59.288
probably it's going to take off again

00:04:59.288 --> 00:05:00.947
as long as you're relaxed.

00:05:00.947 --> 00:05:03.729
But it really is, it's kind
of being on automatic pilot,

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:08.474
and I think it comes after
experience, I think it comes.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.936
And I think I feel in a
happy state of mind now

00:05:10.936 --> 00:05:15.443
that I have 15 years or 20
years of experience behind me

00:05:15.443 --> 00:05:17.819
and I think it's used well

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:19.794
and there's a lot of positive

00:05:19.794 --> 00:05:22.600
out of all the anguish and
the pain and discomfort

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.074
and there have been good times

00:05:24.074 --> 00:05:25.505
and there have been negative times.

00:05:25.505 --> 00:05:28.244
But Olivier said once, when
he was directing Colin Blakely

00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:30.186
in June and the Peacock and
I was in June and the Peacock

00:05:30.186 --> 00:05:32.437
and he said, "You have
to find the middle man."

00:05:32.437 --> 00:05:33.664
And Blakely said, "What do you mean?"

00:05:33.664 --> 00:05:35.016
He said, "Find the middle man,

00:05:35.016 --> 00:05:36.651
"that ease of playing a character."

00:05:36.651 --> 00:05:38.286
And Blakely said, "I only
have until next week."

00:05:38.286 --> 00:05:39.721
And he said, "You won't do it next week,

00:05:39.721 --> 00:05:41.924
"it'll take you the rest of your life."

00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:45.237
And it's really relaxing and letting go.

00:05:45.237 --> 00:05:47.452
You know the booster that
puts you into outer orbit,

00:05:47.452 --> 00:05:49.264
the aggression, the arrogance

00:05:49.264 --> 00:05:50.826
and the ambition and all that,

00:05:50.826 --> 00:05:52.500
that's all very necessary,

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:55.114
but there's a time when one has to let go

00:05:55.114 --> 00:05:57.036
and I guess I'm in orbit

00:05:57.036 --> 00:06:00.442
and all I have to do is rest
assured that it's going to be okay

00:06:00.442 --> 00:06:02.657
and do what is required of me, you know.

00:06:02.657 --> 00:06:05.164
Keep in practice, keep working,

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.434
I'm going back to the theater,

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:08.846
I want to go back to the theater.

00:06:08.846 --> 00:06:11.263
And I'm being kind to myself,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.395
that's all I can say really,

00:06:15.395 --> 00:06:16.915
then the magic happens,

00:06:16.915 --> 00:06:18.171
Scofield is right, you get on with it,

00:06:18.171 --> 00:06:19.848
John Dexter told me in New York, he said,

00:06:19.848 --> 00:06:21.972
"Just get on with it,
don't analyze, do it."

00:06:21.972 --> 00:06:24.309
- What's the most important quality

00:06:24.309 --> 00:06:27.876
that an actor, a great
actor like you, should have?

00:06:27.876 --> 00:06:29.728
What's the most important quality,

00:06:29.728 --> 00:06:31.775
apart from intelligence, I suppose, but?

00:06:31.775 --> 00:06:33.697
- Well, I'm going to be modest,

00:06:33.697 --> 00:06:36.029
I'm a working actor, I
just go from job to job

00:06:36.029 --> 00:06:37.696
and I think there's,

00:06:38.618 --> 00:06:41.333
I have a sense of discipline
and commitment to it

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:43.098
and all those American words, but,

00:06:43.098 --> 00:06:45.578
know what you're doing

00:06:45.578 --> 00:06:47.275
and I have fun with it.

00:06:47.275 --> 00:06:49.524
I always tell that to young
actors I'm working with,

00:06:49.524 --> 00:06:52.921
I say, enjoy it, stop figuring
it all out, just enjoy it.

00:06:52.921 --> 00:06:54.745
If it doesn't work, it doesn't work

00:06:54.745 --> 00:06:56.518
and if you do something
bad it doesn't matter

00:06:56.518 --> 00:06:59.185
and you do something which
may be good, that's good,

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:02.874
but don't worry about it it's
all part of life's process.

00:07:02.874 --> 00:07:05.695
- Nixon must of been one
of the most difficult roles

00:07:05.695 --> 00:07:06.838
you ever played?

00:07:06.838 --> 00:07:09.498
- Rose, that was a
nightmare role to play, yes.

00:07:09.498 --> 00:07:10.854
(laughing)

00:07:10.854 --> 00:07:12.684
I got a phone call in
England many years ago

00:07:12.684 --> 00:07:15.423
and my agent said, "Oliver
Stone wants to talk to you."

00:07:15.423 --> 00:07:17.643
and I said, "Oliver Stone,
what does he want me for?"

00:07:17.643 --> 00:07:19.202
He said, "For Nixon."

00:07:19.202 --> 00:07:20.535
I said, "Nixon?"

00:07:20.535 --> 00:07:22.435
Well he said, "President Nixon."

00:07:22.435 --> 00:07:23.486
I said, "What part?"

00:07:23.486 --> 00:07:24.319
He said, "President Nixon."

00:07:24.319 --> 00:07:26.124
I said "For President
Nixon, are you crazy?"

00:07:26.124 --> 00:07:28.251
I said, "No, he must be mad."

00:07:28.251 --> 00:07:30.472
And he phoned me up and he said,

00:07:30.472 --> 00:07:33.784
"Well, I hear you're chicken,
you don't want to do it."

00:07:33.784 --> 00:07:36.119
I said, "Well, I don't want
to do you a disservice."

00:07:36.119 --> 00:07:38.124
He said, "Well I'm
coming into London anyway

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:40.516
"at the beginning of next
week so lets meet anyway

00:07:40.516 --> 00:07:41.866
"even though you don't want to do it."

00:07:41.866 --> 00:07:42.969
I said, "Okay."

00:07:42.969 --> 00:07:45.181
So I was on my way to
the hotel to meet him

00:07:45.181 --> 00:07:47.099
and I had that moment of clarity

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:50.216
when I, in the middle of Hyde Park,

00:07:50.216 --> 00:07:52.185
and I thought I can either work

00:07:52.185 --> 00:07:54.846
with this great American director,

00:07:54.846 --> 00:07:56.646
make a complete idiot of myself,

00:07:56.646 --> 00:08:00.091
or I can stay safe here in
Britain working for the BBC,

00:08:00.091 --> 00:08:03.036
go off to Hungary to make a
Dostoevsky film or something,

00:08:03.036 --> 00:08:04.825
something boring like that.

00:08:04.825 --> 00:08:05.658
(audience laughing)

00:08:05.658 --> 00:08:07.159
And you know stay happy
for the rest of my life

00:08:07.159 --> 00:08:09.258
and die of a heart attack
and that'll be the end of it,

00:08:09.258 --> 00:08:10.959
but I thought well, I'll just do something

00:08:10.959 --> 00:08:12.433
that's really challenging.

00:08:12.433 --> 00:08:14.761
So I met Oliver Stone for
breakfast that very morning,

00:08:14.761 --> 00:08:17.912
and half an hour later
I said, "I'll do it."

00:08:17.912 --> 00:08:19.121
He said, "Great."

00:08:19.121 --> 00:08:21.913
So there we were and
I believe that be bold

00:08:21.913 --> 00:08:24.228
and mighty forces will come to your aid

00:08:24.228 --> 00:08:25.655
and I believe that about
everything, you know,

00:08:25.655 --> 00:08:28.076
so I don't do anything
that's conventional.

00:08:28.076 --> 00:08:29.863
When I approached magic I just showed up,

00:08:29.863 --> 00:08:31.883
I did a lot of preparation,

00:08:31.883 --> 00:08:33.765
all I have to do is be ready I guess

00:08:33.765 --> 00:08:36.231
and I try to apply it to my life now

00:08:36.231 --> 00:08:37.914
and I just have to get ready, you know.

00:08:37.914 --> 00:08:40.032
I just have to do what is asked of me

00:08:40.032 --> 00:08:43.965
and do as much as I can
without driving myself insane,

00:08:43.965 --> 00:08:46.920
because there's a negative
side of perfectionism.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.418
In my nature anyway, I
can only speak for myself.

00:08:49.418 --> 00:08:52.237
There's a negative flaw and
that is a very dangerous trap

00:08:52.237 --> 00:08:55.938
and I think that one of
the biggest killers is ego

00:08:55.938 --> 00:08:58.389
and whence the negative
side of perfectionism,

00:08:58.389 --> 00:09:00.560
when one starts playing God, you know,

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.096
and I mean literally, that it is a killer,

00:09:03.096 --> 00:09:07.240
that it is a lethal part of one owns ego.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:09.662
I went to the movies and I saw Brando

00:09:09.662 --> 00:09:11.303
and I became an actor.

00:09:11.303 --> 00:09:15.470
I saw James Dean and I always
felt I wanted to be like that,

00:09:16.379 --> 00:09:18.841
but I thought I'm stuck
with a funny accent

00:09:18.841 --> 00:09:21.299
in this place in Britain

00:09:21.299 --> 00:09:24.502
and then I read Jack Kerouac's On the Road

00:09:24.502 --> 00:09:28.225
and I read Look Homeward
Angel, I was about 19 or 20,

00:09:28.225 --> 00:09:30.825
something like that and I
had this taste for America.

00:09:30.825 --> 00:09:35.080
And I had this taste for
rebellion and the darkness

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.895
and so this is what I wanted
to do more than anything

00:09:38.895 --> 00:09:40.825
and when I came over to America

00:09:40.825 --> 00:09:44.057
I made a couple of good films
and some not so good films,

00:09:44.057 --> 00:09:47.700
but I wanted to make a statement
for myself on this one,

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.856
not for anyone, but for
myself, to prove it to myself

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:52.611
that I had that in me.

00:09:52.611 --> 00:09:54.244
I'm going to be 70 at the end of the year,

00:09:54.244 --> 00:09:56.661
that I had that something so off the wall

00:09:56.661 --> 00:09:59.408
and wacko that I could
put it on screen some how

00:09:59.408 --> 00:10:00.609
and that's why I did it.

00:10:00.609 --> 00:10:02.086
I don't know if believe in anything,

00:10:02.086 --> 00:10:06.659
I mean what deity, but I
believe whatever that thing is

00:10:06.659 --> 00:10:08.989
that we talk about for centuries,

00:10:08.989 --> 00:10:10.757
I think it's just within us.

00:10:10.757 --> 00:10:14.130
I mean remarkable things
have happened in my life

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.955
by just wishing or asking for something,

00:10:16.955 --> 00:10:18.387
for a bit of help here

00:10:18.387 --> 00:10:21.540
and I don't believe,
I'm an agnostic I guess.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:24.001
I say, is there anyway you
can help me, or whatever?

00:10:24.001 --> 00:10:26.908
And there's something inside
that will respond I believe,

00:10:26.908 --> 00:10:28.457
I really believe that.

00:10:28.457 --> 00:10:30.952
We have to make our lives
because life is tough,

00:10:30.952 --> 00:10:33.853
we have to believe in the power of life.

00:10:33.853 --> 00:10:35.363
- Now, okay let's talk about this movie.

00:10:35.363 --> 00:10:39.618
You're a priest, then you're
trying to convince this guy

00:10:39.618 --> 00:10:41.631
that doesn't really believe

00:10:41.631 --> 00:10:43.873
and then all of a sudden
you become possessed--

00:10:43.873 --> 00:10:44.706
- That's right.

00:10:44.706 --> 00:10:45.539
- By the devil.

00:10:45.539 --> 00:10:47.941
You are a good devil.

00:10:47.941 --> 00:10:48.841
(audience laughing)

00:10:48.841 --> 00:10:49.750
You are.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.013
(audience laughing)

00:10:52.013 --> 00:10:53.853
I mean that in the kindest way.

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:54.930
- Yeah, thank you my dear.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.146
(audience laughing)

00:10:56.146 --> 00:10:57.423
- I mean really you
play a bad guy so good,

00:10:57.423 --> 00:10:59.104
when you turned, cause your
character's not like that

00:10:59.104 --> 00:11:00.163
for the first part of the movie.

00:11:00.163 --> 00:11:00.996
- He's a good man.

00:11:00.996 --> 00:11:02.245
- Then all of a sudden you're--

00:11:02.245 --> 00:11:03.310
- Suddenly he becomes nuts.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.146
- And then suddenly you become very--

00:11:05.146 --> 00:11:06.220
- Yeah, very strange.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.823
I don't know why they
cast me in these parts?

00:11:07.823 --> 00:11:08.656
I have no idea.

00:11:08.656 --> 00:11:09.791
(audience laughing)

00:11:09.791 --> 00:11:10.624
- [Ellen] No?

00:11:10.624 --> 00:11:13.392
- But I mean I've no idea
because I'm not like that at all.

00:11:13.392 --> 00:11:14.410
(audience laughing)

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:17.158
- See look, just doing
that is scary to me.

00:11:17.158 --> 00:11:20.067
(audience laughing and applauding)

00:11:20.067 --> 00:11:22.198
- I've got a technique,
I don't know what it is,

00:11:22.198 --> 00:11:24.155
I honestly don't know, seriously.

00:11:24.155 --> 00:11:25.344
People say how do you do that?

00:11:25.344 --> 00:11:27.356
I have no idea, I just do it.

00:11:27.356 --> 00:11:28.189
(audience laughing)

00:11:28.189 --> 00:11:29.919
- Like right now, just look at the camera

00:11:29.919 --> 00:11:32.493
and make a scary, scary face.

00:11:32.493 --> 00:11:33.476
- Oh,

00:11:33.476 --> 00:11:34.865
(audience laughing)

00:11:34.865 --> 00:11:36.666
- [Ellen] That's really creepy.

00:11:36.666 --> 00:11:38.227
(audience laughing)

00:11:38.227 --> 00:11:39.624
- You just deaden the eyes, that's all.

00:11:39.624 --> 00:11:40.457
- Yeah, it is.

00:11:40.457 --> 00:11:41.303
- Don't blink,

00:11:41.303 --> 00:11:42.934
but I don't know, it's
called acting I guess.

00:11:42.934 --> 00:11:45.022
But I'm not like that inside, at all.

00:11:45.022 --> 00:11:46.045
(audience laughing)

00:11:46.045 --> 00:11:47.835
(all laughing)

00:11:47.835 --> 00:11:50.138
(audience laughing)

00:11:50.138 --> 00:11:51.055
Not at all.

00:11:52.409 --> 00:11:56.115
Life is just terrific, I travel the world

00:11:56.115 --> 00:11:57.804
and I'm still working

00:11:57.804 --> 00:12:00.216
and working with some interesting people

00:12:00.216 --> 00:12:03.821
and people think it's, you know, a dream.

00:12:03.821 --> 00:12:05.738
But there are problems,

00:12:07.113 --> 00:12:10.696
you know I pay a few
people to help me and,

00:12:14.192 --> 00:12:17.359
my wife has a friend called Juan Arias

00:12:18.362 --> 00:12:20.163
and she called him Johnny on the spot,

00:12:20.163 --> 00:12:22.286
my wife Stella, Johnny on the spot,

00:12:22.286 --> 00:12:24.369
means Johnny on the spot,

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:31.826
except this guy is rarely on the spot,

00:12:31.826 --> 00:12:33.341
sometimes you can't even find him,

00:12:33.341 --> 00:12:34.953
he's supposed to be my personal assistant.

00:12:34.953 --> 00:12:35.978
Can you believe that?

00:12:35.978 --> 00:12:39.173
I pay him lots of money,
it's really shocking,

00:12:39.173 --> 00:12:41.590
but well that's life I guess.

00:12:45.762 --> 00:12:48.254
Be quiet cause I'll introduce you,

00:12:48.254 --> 00:12:51.663
I'll show you Johnny on the spot.

00:12:51.663 --> 00:12:52.830
There you are.

00:12:56.026 --> 00:12:59.193
That's him, that's Johnny on the spot,

00:13:00.602 --> 00:13:03.685
paid a lot of money and he's useless,

00:13:05.408 --> 00:13:06.241
useless.

00:13:07.456 --> 00:13:10.873
My cat Niblo would be a better assistant,

00:13:12.157 --> 00:13:13.975
but what can you do, you win them all,

00:13:13.975 --> 00:13:16.444
my life's not perfect you know,

00:13:16.444 --> 00:13:18.161
I don't know how to get rid of him,

00:13:18.161 --> 00:13:20.323
but anyway, that's John,

00:13:20.323 --> 00:13:24.323
first-class private travel,
private hotel rooms,

00:13:25.853 --> 00:13:28.308
all the women hug him on set,

00:13:28.308 --> 00:13:30.639
they don't even know who I am,

00:13:30.639 --> 00:13:32.569
but anyway that's life.

00:13:32.569 --> 00:13:36.734
It's not all roses in the movie business.

00:13:36.734 --> 00:13:37.567
Yeah,

00:13:38.544 --> 00:13:39.711
that was good.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.501
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:44.501 --> 00:13:47.335
I made this video because
Kendrick Bowman asked me to.

00:13:47.335 --> 00:13:49.053
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:13:49.053 --> 00:13:50.241
that you want me to profile next,

00:13:50.241 --> 00:13:51.519
leave it down in the comments below

00:13:51.519 --> 00:13:52.715
and I'll see what I can do.

00:13:52.715 --> 00:13:54.190
I'd also love to know what did you learn

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:55.578
from Anthony Hopkins today

00:13:55.578 --> 00:13:57.665
that you're going to apply
in immediately to your life

00:13:57.665 --> 00:13:58.728
or your business?

00:13:58.728 --> 00:14:00.284
What was your favorite rule and why?

00:14:00.284 --> 00:14:02.952
Leave it the comments, I'm
going to join in the discussion.

00:14:02.952 --> 00:14:04.632
Finally I want to give a quick shout out

00:14:04.632 --> 00:14:05.842
to the LonelyBookaneer,

00:14:05.842 --> 00:14:07.770
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:09.689
Your One Word and taking that picture

00:14:09.689 --> 00:14:12.481
and posting it to Instagram,
those cookies look delicious

00:14:12.481 --> 00:14:14.777
and I really, really
appreciate your support.

00:14:14.777 --> 00:14:17.317
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:14:17.317 --> 00:14:19.410
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:22.289
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:14:22.289 --> 00:14:23.789
I'll see you soon.

00:14:30.931 --> 00:14:32.903
- What has happened in
some strange circuitous way

00:14:32.903 --> 00:14:35.887
on this journey through
life is that I've become

00:14:35.887 --> 00:14:38.626
more at peace with myself.

00:14:38.626 --> 00:14:40.887
I suppose we compensate for our lives,

00:14:40.887 --> 00:14:43.470
for our lacks, if we choose to,

00:14:44.379 --> 00:14:46.649
because I felt so lacking as a child

00:14:46.649 --> 00:14:48.203
and in my adolescent years

00:14:48.203 --> 00:14:50.090
and early adult years

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:53.337
I through anger, resentment or drive

00:14:53.337 --> 00:14:54.855
or ambition or whatever,

00:14:54.855 --> 00:14:57.233
I found my way, somehow.

00:14:57.233 --> 00:14:59.733
I don't actually believe I
did it totally on my own,

00:14:59.733 --> 00:15:03.269
I believe in some power
of life that is in us.

00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:05.519
I'm a fatalist, I believe in destiny,

00:15:05.519 --> 00:15:08.379
I believe if we relax and let go enough

00:15:08.379 --> 00:15:10.467
and actually do believe that our lives

00:15:10.467 --> 00:15:11.863
our none of our business

00:15:11.863 --> 00:15:14.640
and open up then extraordinary
things begin to happen.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.427
I suppose you could be calling
them spiritual surrender

00:15:17.427 --> 00:15:19.847
or something of the
sort, now when we try to,

00:15:19.847 --> 00:15:22.996
I mean my agent many, many
years ago, I had an agent once,

00:15:22.996 --> 00:15:26.777
very nice chap but he said,
"We've got to plan your career."

00:15:26.777 --> 00:15:28.659
I mean that sent me running out the door,

00:15:28.659 --> 00:15:29.850
you can't plan your life.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.567
- No, I wouldn't care for that.

00:15:31.567 --> 00:15:33.780
- You make certain
choices and you go along

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.884
and you, you know, you chart
the rapids and the rocks

00:15:37.884 --> 00:15:41.531
and the shallows and the
depths and so on and so forth,

00:15:41.531 --> 00:15:43.531
but you can't really control your destiny,

00:15:43.531 --> 00:15:44.979
you can't really control things,

00:15:44.979 --> 00:15:46.348
you just have to let go and follow it.

